  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-23T01:03:27.011Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've been doing a lot of troubleshooting with my avatars tail to try and make it react closer to how it did with dynamic bones. While trying to reproduce  the way the tail would lay on the ground collider, i encountered a new issue where the tail was jittering and bouncing along the collider. This was also happening in game with just dyn bone to phys bone conversion. While in unity i wanted to troubleshoot and see if i could get rid of the jitter. The only thing i can tell causing the issue was the \"immobilize\" slider. Whenever it is set to a value greater than 0, my tail would jitter around. Which is unfortunate as i want to keep it around 0.8 to keep my tails movement down while locomoting.",
